# Parameterized ADT alias: [type [let a] Ok: [value: a] Error: [msg: String]] must
# register with one type parameter, enabling correct instantiation at each use site.
# Both constructors are injected: Ok (polymorphic on a) and Error (takes String).
# At runtime: constructors appear in the type dict as callable functions.
[
  Result: [type [let a] Ok: [value: a] Error: [msg: String]]
  v1: [Result.Ok value: 99]
  v2: [Result.Error msg: "oops"]
]
=== out
Dict({"Result": Dict({"Ok": Function(value), "Error": Function(msg)}), "v1": Variant(Result.Ok, Dict({"value": Int(99)})), "v2": Variant(Result.Error, Dict({"msg": String("oops")}))})
